 [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec2ee41e0de0c712ef8cfebd047f3cccceb49e4ff090131273e0299416cd0b5a"} {"question" "q-11572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec2ee41e0de0c712ef8cfebd047f3cccceb49e4ff090131273e0299416cd0b5a"} {"question" "e-4401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $AB$ and $BA,$ if \n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-4401.json" "file_sha256" "130a347366d6cc521a98a2525ae45705a5425abe282fba7ea5ced39e91e8c62c"} {"question" "e-4401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot (-1) & 1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2 \\\\ -5\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1) & -5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-5) & -1\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ -11 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** Notice that \n\n$$\nAB \\neq BA.\n$$\n\nMatrix multiplication is not **commutative**, meaning that when we switch the order of multiplication, we often get a different result (like we did in this example)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-4401.json" "file_sha256" "130a347366d6cc521a98a2525ae45705a5425abe282fba7ea5ced39e91e8c62c"} {"question" "e-5255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $Z=XY.$ What is the value of $z_{32}$, if\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-5255.json" "file_sha256" "f9fdf6f4e7ee28b503083867424e562abff332d2f4d00fae68a62694cb970849"} {"question" "e-5255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $X$ by the $2$nd column in $Y$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}_{32} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-1+8-6 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-5255.json" "file_sha256" "f9fdf6f4e7ee28b503083867424e562abff332d2f4d00fae68a62694cb970849"} {"question" "e-4402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $AB$, if \n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-4402.json" "file_sha256" "ddcefab4accf9604577626e3f787ba05bcc6fb0b27771bf772dbfcd52866f4e0"} {"question" "e-4402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+0-9 & -6+0-3 & 4+0+6 \\\\ 0-1+6 & 9+2+2 & -6-4-4 \\\\ 0+0+3 & -6+0+1 & 4+0-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 13 & -14 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-4402.json" "file_sha256" "ddcefab4accf9604577626e3f787ba05bcc6fb0b27771bf772dbfcd52866f4e0"}] "usage" {"q-68290" [] "e-5255" [] "e-4401" [] "e-4402" []} "basis" 762 "retractions" [[17592186060309 :question/problem "Let $C = AB$. What is the value of $c_{21}$, if\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$?"] [17592186059479 :question/problem "Find $AB$ and $BA$, if\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059479 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot (-1) & 1 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot 2 \\\\ -5 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot (-1) & -5 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nBA &= \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot (-5) & 0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 1 \\\\ -1 \\cdot 1 + 2 \\cdot (-5) & -1 \\cdot 0 + 2 \\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ -11 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** Notice that\n\n$$\nAB \\neq BA\n$$\n\nMatrix multiplication is not **commutative**, meaning that when we switch the order of multiplication, we often get a different result (like we did in this example)."] [17592186059523 :question/problem "Let $Z=XY$. What is the value of $z_{32}$, if\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059523 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $X$ by the $2$nd column in $Y$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz_{32} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (-1) + 2 \\cdot 4 + 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&=-1 + 8 - 6 \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059480 :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186059480 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 + 0 - 9 & -6 + 0 - 3 & 4 + 0 + 6 \\\\ 0 - 1 + 6 & 9 + 2 + 2 & -6 - 4 - 4 \\\\ 0 + 0 + 3 & -6 + 0 + 1 & 4 + 0 - 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 13 & -14 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186058838 17592186058839 17592186058840 17592186058841 17592186058842] "immutable_fields" [[17592186058837 :answer-field/correct] [17592186058837 :answer-field/id] [175